    "\n",
    "class_weights = dict(zip(classes, class_weights))"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "9b0725ac",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Model Implementation Strategies in Churn Prediction\n",
    "\n",
    "In this section, we implement and compare multiple modeling approaches to predict customer churn."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "6ea94714",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 2.1 Keras Artificial Neural Network (ANN) Model\n",
    "\n",
    "Our first ANN model is the TensorFlow/Keras's Sequential API. We define a network with at least two hidden layers and batch normalisation for regularisation and training stability. We also include 2 dropouts for generalisation.\n",
    "\n",
    "_**Notice that in the model, we also chose AUPRC metrics for future optimisation, in order to handle imbalanced data, minimise both false positives and false negatives.**_"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "5f1cb482",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 2.1.1 Using Hyperband for Keras Model Tuning\n",
    "\n",
    "In this section of tuning, we use `Hyperband` for our keras model, as it uses the least resource to train the top promising models. Once it reach its maximum performance, we insert a callback to stop training."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 16,
   "id": "9b59d208",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Early stop for validation loss\n",
    "early_stop = EarlyStopping(monitor='val_loss', patience=10, restore_best_weights=True)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 17,
   "id": "33ec8612",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Initiate model class\n",
    "ann = ANN_tf(input_dim=X_train_full.shape[1])\n",
    "\n",
    "def hypermodel(hp): \n",
    "    return ann.model_keras(hp)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 18,
   "id": "094d337f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Trial 90 Complete [00h 01m 40s]\n",
      "val_auprc: 0.6388251980145773\n",
      "\n",
      "Best val_auprc So Far: 0.6548075278600057\n",
      "Total elapsed time: 00h 53m 36s\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Force directory refresh\n",
    "shutil.rmtree('hyperband', ignore_errors=True) \n",
    "\n",
    "# Hyperband tuner and search\n",
    "HBtuner = Hyperband(\n",
    "    hypermodel,\n",
    "    max_epochs=30,\n",
    "    objective=Objective(\"val_auprc\", direction=\"max\"),\n",
    "    executions_per_trial=3,\n",
    "    directory='hyperband',\n",
    "    project_name='krs_hyperband',\n",
    "    overwrite=True)\n",
    "\n",
    "HBtuner.search(X_train_full, y_train_full, validation_data=(X_valid, y_valid), callbacks=[early_stop], verbose=1)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "67b79b8c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 2.2.2 Model Rebuild with Best Hyperparameters\n",
    "Compare with the churner rate 0.26, a validation AUPRC with around 0.65 shows that the model could correctly find more churners and not wrongly flagging loyal customers. After optimising auprc, we decided to filter out the trials with accuracies that didn't meet a specified threshold (<0.78) and keep the rest for model rebuild. Since we are no longer using keras tuner, we would have to replace the undefined hyperparameter (hp) with `units1`, `units2`, `lr` from our initial model, as well as the `hp.Int(...)` and `hp.Float(...)` from the layers."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 19,
   "id": "1847ca9f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# Get best params from hyperband\n",
    "def get_best_params(tuner, keys=(\"units1\", \"units2\", \"units3\", \"lr\")):\n",
    "    all_trials = [t for t in tuner.oracle.get_best_trials() if t.status == \"COMPLETED\"]\n",
    "    candidate = [t for t in all_trials\n",
    "                 if t.metrics.get_last_value(\"val_accuracy\") is not None\n",
    "                 and t.metrics.get_last_value(\"val_accuracy\") >= 0.78 \n",
    "                 and t.metrics.get_last_value(\"val_auprc\") is not None]\n",
    "    if not candidate:\n",
    "        hp = tuner.get_best_hyperparameters(num_trials=1)[0]\n",
    "        return {k: hp.get(k) for k in keys}\n",
    "    best = max(candidate, key=lambda t: t.metrics.get_last_value(\"val_auprc\"))\n",
    "    hp_vals = best.hyperparameters.values\n",
    "    return {k: hp_vals[k] for k in keys}"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 20,
   "id": "a676aa7d-61a5-4fbe-912f-b44be795c399",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Selected parameters:  {'units1': 128, 'units2': 64, 'units3': 16, 'lr': 0.000134820344475202}\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Call function to retrieve best parameters that also meet threshold\n",
    "best_params = get_best_params(HBtuner)\n",
    "print(\"Selected parameters: \", best_params)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 23,
   "id": "38a482c1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Training time: 30.0 seconds\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Trian model\n",
    "start = time.time()\n",
    "model = ann.model_rebuild(**best_params)\n",
    "history = model.fit(X_train_full, y_train_full, \n",
    "                    validation_data=(X_valid, y_valid), \n",
    "                    epochs=50, \n",
    "                    callbacks=[early_stop], \n",
    "                    verbose=0)\n",
    "elapsed = time.time() - start\n",
    "print(f\"Training time: {elapsed:.1f} seconds\")"
   ]
